1 Introduction
**************

‘mab-org.el’ bundles the helpers used to assemble manuscript-style
modular annotated bibliographies (mab) and lighter-weight annotated
bibliographies (abib) inside Org-mode buffers.

   The package wraps citar (and ebib) citekeys with LaTeX ‘\bibentry’
code, creates per-citekey Org notes from a configurable template,
optionally appends BibTeX entries to a project-specific ‘.bib’ file, and
bulk applies the same wrapping to every citation in a region.  It also
stamps out a fresh ‘mab<NUMBER>/mab<NUMBER>.org’ project file from a
built-in template, finds or creates such a file by project number, and
appends a wrapped block to the project file directly from inside ‘ebib’.

   When a per-citekey note already exists (for example because it was
created during work on another project), the package detects the
duplicate and offers to reuse the existing note, create a variant with
the next available letter suffix, or quit without changing the buffer.


