3 Installation
**************

3.1 Manual
==========

Put the directory on your ‘load-path’ and load the package.

     (add-to-list 'load-path "/path/to/mab-org/")
     (require 'mab-org)

3.2 With ‘use-package’
======================

     (use-package mab-org
       :load-path "/path/to/mab-org/"
       :commands (mab-org-create-project
                  mab-org-open-file
                  mab-org-wrap-citekey
                  mab-org-wrap-citekey-abib
                  mab-org-wrap-region
                  mab-org-insert-matching-keys
                  mab-org-add-bib-item))

3.3 From a system ‘make install’
================================

*Note Makefile Targets::, for a description of ‘make install’ and ‘make
install-info’.  Both honor a ‘PREFIX’ variable so the files can be
staged anywhere under your home directory.


