4 Configuration
***************

The package exposes user options through the customization group
‘mab-org’.  Customize them with ‘M-x customize-group RET mab-org RET’ or
set them in your init file.

 -- User Option: mab-org-notes-directory
     Directory that holds per-citekey Org notes.  Default
     ‘~/abibNotes/’.

 -- User Option: mab-org-pdfs-directory
     Directory that holds renamed article PDFs.  Default
     ‘~/0papersLabeled/’.

 -- User Option: mab-org-books-directory
     Directory that holds renamed book PDFs.  A second file link is
     added to every wrapped block so notes derived from books are
     reachable without changing the template.  Default
     ‘~/0booksLabeled/’.

 -- User Option: mab-org-global-bib-file
     Path to the global BibTeX library, searched by
     ‘mab-org-insert-matching-keys’.  Default ‘~/Documents/global.bib’.

 -- User Option: mab-org-region-confirm-threshold
     Maximum number of citations a region may carry before
     ‘mab-org-wrap-region’ asks for confirmation.  Default 10.

 -- User Option: mab-org-book-entry-regexp
     Regexp identifying a BibTeX entry that should use the book PDF link
     instead of the article PDF link.  Matched against the raw entry
     text (case-insensitively).  The default is
     ‘"\\`[[:space:]]*@book"’, which catches ‘@book’ and ‘@booklet’
     through prefix match.  Extend it to also catch ‘@inbook’ or
     ‘@incollection’ when needed.

 -- User Option: mab-org-base-directory
     Default base directory under which mab project files live.  When
     nil, ‘mab-org-create-project’ falls back to the directory of the
     current buffer (or ‘default-directory’ when there is no buffer
     file).

 -- User Option: mab-org-mab-path
     Default destination for ‘mab-org-add-bib-item’.  This is the
     absolute path of the mab project Org file to which ebib entries are
     appended.  When nil, the user is prompted with no default.  The
     variable is updated automatically when ‘mab-org-add-bib-item’ is
     called interactively, so the most recent choice persists for the
     rest of the session.


