7 Variant Resolution
********************

When ‘mab-org-wrap-citekey’ or ‘mab-org-wrap-citekey-abib’ detects an
existing ‘<citekey>.org’ in ‘mab-org-notes-directory’, it asks the user
how to proceed:

‘r’ (reuse)
     Keep the existing note.  No new file is written; the wrapped block
     references the existing note.

‘v’ (variant)
     Create a new note whose stem has the next available lowercase
     letter appended.  For example, if ‘Foo2020Bar.org’ already exists,
     the new stem becomes ‘Foo2020Bara’; if ‘Foo2020Bara.org’ also
     exists, the next stem is ‘Foo2020Barb’.

‘q’ (quit)
     Abort without changing the buffer.  No file is written, no text is
     inserted.

   What the variant suffix changes:

   • The ‘\addcontentsline’ table-of-contents entry uses the stem, so a
     variant gets a distinct row in the TOC.
   • The ‘#+INCLUDE:’ directive and the Org-note link use the stem, so
     the variant note is the file actually opened and included.
   • The ‘\bibentry’ command and the article and book PDF links keep the
     original citekey, because the BibTeX library and the PDF/book
     archives are keyed by citekey.


