8 Ebib Integration
******************

The package integrates with ‘ebib’ via ‘mab-org-add-bib-item’.  The
command must be invoked from an ‘ebib’ index buffer; outside it the
command signals ‘user-error’.

   Once ‘ebib’ is loaded, the package binds the command to ‘B’:

     (eval-after-load 'ebib
       '(when (boundp 'ebib-index-mode-map)
          (define-key ebib-index-mode-map (kbd "B") #'mab-org-add-bib-item)))

   The flow:

  1. Open ebib (‘M-x ebib’) and navigate to the entry you want to
     annotate.

  2. Press ‘B’.

  3. Confirm the destination mab project file (default
     ‘mab-org-mab-path’, if set, otherwise prompt with no default).

  4. The package writes the wrapped block under the section
     ‘\section*{Illustrated and annotated bibliography}’, appended just
     below the last existing entry and above any ‘\clearpage’ (and
     surrounding blank lines) that introduces the
     ‘\section*{Backmatter}’ heading, so the entry stays inside the
     bibliography section in the rendered document.  An empty
     per-citekey abibnote is created if none exists yet.


