9 The Test Suite
****************

The companion file ‘mab-org-test.el’ carries an ERT regression suite for
the package.

9.1 What the suite covers
=========================

   • Citekey extraction from the three accepted forms (‘[cite:@KEY]’,
     ‘[cite:@a,@b]’, bare word, nil).

   • Default project number detection from filenames (‘mab<N>.org’,
     ‘ab<N>.org’, bare digits, no digits, nil).

   • mab-style and abib-style wrapped text rendering, including the
     default-to-article behavior, the ‘book-p’ switch to the books
     directory, and the variant-stem split that keeps the bibentry and
     PDF link on the citekey while INCLUDE/TOC/note link follow the
     stem.

   • ‘mab-org--book-entry-p’ predicate, including the default ‘@book’
     prefix match and a custom regexp that adds ‘@inbook’ and
     ‘@incollection’.

   • ‘mab-org--lookup-bibtex-entry’ fallback to
     ‘mab-org-global-bib-file’ when citar is not loaded.

   • Region citation collection and ordering.

   • Empty-note creation, including missing-directory creation, and not
     overwriting an existing note.

   • Variant resolution: no existing note (no prompt), reuse, variant,
     all letters taken (variant option suppressed), quit (signals
     ‘user-error’).

   • Project template substitution and project file creation, including
     the ‘mab<N>/’ subdirectory layout, refusal to overwrite, and nested
     base directory creation.

   • BibTeX append helper (creates new file, preserves existing
     content).

   • Bounds detection (citation block versus bare word at point).

   • The search-and-insert command against an in-memory ‘global.bib’.

   • ‘mab-org-add-bib-item’ insertion behavior with and without a
     Backmatter section, with the new entry placed above any
     ‘\clearpage’ that introduces Backmatter, the missing-section error,
     the rejected non-ebib buffer error, and automatic note creation.

   • Public command surface: every command listed in *note Public
     Commands:: is bound and interactive.

9.2 Helpers used by the suite
=============================

 -- Function: mab-org-test--with-temp-dir fn
     Call FN with the path to a fresh temporary directory.  The
     directory and its contents are deleted after FN returns.

 -- Macro: mab-org-test-with-temp-dir var &rest body
     Bind VAR to a fresh temporary directory and evaluate BODY.

 -- Function: mab-org-test--read-file path
     Return the contents of PATH as a string.

 -- Function: mab-org-test--make-mab-file path &optional with-backmatter
     Write a minimal mab Org file to PATH for testing.  When
     WITH-BACKMATTER is non-nil, also include a Backmatter section after
     the bibliography heading.

9.3 Mocking ebib and read-multiple-choice
=========================================

The suite uses ‘cl-letf’ to mock ‘read-multiple-choice’ for the
variant-resolution tests, and ‘ebib--get-key-at-point’ together with
‘derived-mode-p’ for the ebib-integration tests.  This means the suite
runs without ‘ebib’ or ‘citar’ installed.

9.4 Running the suite
=====================

     make test

   The Makefile target removes any stale ‘.elc’ before running so Emacs
cannot accidentally load an out-of-date byte-compiled definition.  *Note
Makefile Targets::.


