10 Makefile Targets
*******************

The Makefile uses GNU-style installation variables that you can override
on the command line.

Variable           Default
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
‘PREFIX’           ‘$(HOME)/.local’
‘INFODIR’          ‘$(PREFIX)/share/info’
‘EMACSDIR’         ‘$(PREFIX)/share/emacs/site-lisp’
‘EMACS’            ‘emacs’
‘INSTALL’          ‘install’
‘INSTALL_INFO’     ‘install-info’

‘make all’
     The default target.  Equivalent to ‘make compile test’.

‘make test’
     Run the ERT suite in batch mode.  Removes stale ‘.elc’ first so
     Emacs cannot load an outdated byte-compiled definition.

‘make compile’
     Byte-compile ‘mab-org.el’ to ‘mab-org.elc’.

‘make info’
     Build ‘mab-org.info’ from ‘mab-org.texi’ with ‘makeinfo’.

‘make install’
     Install ‘mab-org.el’ into ‘$(EMACSDIR)’.  Override ‘PREFIX’ to
     choose another location.

‘make install-info’
     Build ‘mab-org.info’ (if necessary) and install it into
     ‘$(INFODIR)’, then run ‘install-info’ so the page is registered
     with ‘info’'s top-level directory.

‘make uninstall’
     Remove the installed ‘mab-org.el’ from ‘$(EMACSDIR)’.

‘make uninstall-info’
     Remove the installed ‘mab-org.info’ from ‘$(INFODIR)’ and
     unregister it from the top-level directory.

‘make lint’
     Run ‘checkdoc’ against ‘mab-org.el’.

‘make clean’
     Remove all build products, including ‘.elc’ and ‘.info’.

   A typical user-level install:

     make
     make install
     make install-info

   A typical system install (with ‘sudo’):

     sudo make PREFIX=/usr/local install install-info


