12 Changelog
************

*0.4.0*
     Replaced the two PDF lines in the wrapped block with a single PDF
     link.  The link points at ‘mab-org-pdfs-directory’ by default and
     at ‘mab-org-books-directory’ when the BibTeX entry matches
     ‘mab-org-book-entry-regexp’ (default: ‘@book’ prefix).  Added
     ‘mab-org--lookup-bibtex-entry’ which tries citar first and falls
     back to ‘mab-org-global-bib-file’, and added
     ‘mab-org--book-entry-p’.

*0.3.2*
     Removed the ‘:Notes:’ ...  ‘:END:’ drawer and the "Add more prose.
     Add tables.  Add figures."  line from the mab-style wrapped block.
     The three file links (to the per-note Org file, the article PDF,
     and the book PDF) are retained and now appear as bare lines.
     Reworked ‘mab-org-add-bib-item’ so the new entry is appended above
     any ‘\clearpage’ that introduces the Backmatter section, so entries
     stay inside the bibliography section in the rendered document.

*0.3.1*
     Removed the per-citekey note template.  New abibnotes are created
     empty.  Dropped ‘mab-org-note-template’ and
     ‘mab-org-create-note-files’.

*0.3.0*
     Renamed the package from ‘mab’ to ‘mab-org’.  Adopted the
     ‘mab<NUMBER>/’ subdirectory convention for project files.  Added
     ‘mab-org-add-bib-item’ for ebib integration, ‘mab-org-open-file’
     for find-or-create, and ‘mab-org-books-directory’ so wrapped blocks
     include a book PDF link.

*0.2.0*
     Added the variant-note prompt (reuse, variant, quit) for duplicate
     abibnotes, an alphabet-walking next-letter helper, and the
     two-argument render functions that accept a stem distinct from the
     citekey.

*0.1.0*
     Initial collection: wrap a citekey, wrap a region, search the
     global bib, and stamp out a project file from a template.


