13 MELPA Notes
**************

The package follows the conventions checked by ‘package-build’ and
‘package-lint’:

   • ‘lexical-binding: t’ declared on the first line.
   • Standard package header with ‘Author’, ‘Maintainer’, ‘URL’,
     ‘Version’, ‘Package-Requires’, and ‘Keywords’.
   • A trailing ‘;;; mab-org.el ends here’ marker.
   • ‘(provide 'mab-org)’ is the last form in the file.
   • Every public symbol is prefixed with ‘mab-org-’; every internal
     symbol is prefixed with ‘mab-org--’.
   • ‘;;;###autoload’ cookies on the public commands.
   • ‘(require 'bibtex)’ declares the only mandatory dependency
     explicitly.  ‘citar’ and ‘ebib’ are optional and are detected at
     runtime via ‘(featurep 'citar)’ and ‘(eval-after-load 'ebib ...)’.

   This Texinfo file is built by ‘make info’ and produces
‘mab-org.info’, which carries the ‘@dircategory Emacs’ and ‘@direntry’
required to register the page with ‘info’'s top-level directory.  The
MELPA recipe should list the ‘.texi’ (and the resulting ‘.info’) under
‘:files’ when an info-installable build is desired.


